{
  "id": "ja-nein-fragen",
  "name": "Yes/no questions and negation with no",
  "level": "A1",
  "variety": "es-ES",
  "subtitle": "A yes/no question can use the same words as a statement. Only ¿…? in writing and your voice going up show that it is a question. Put no before the verb to say “not”.",
  "briefMarks": ["¿…?", "sí", "no"],
  "source": "icanspeak Spanish original text (grammar-a1 run, 2026-11-04)",
  "concept": {
    "flow": [
      { "text": "¿", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "(person)" },
      { "text": "verb", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "rest ?" }
    ],
    "exampleHtml": "Ana trabaja hoy. → ¿Ana <span class=\"vp-verb\">trabaja</span> hoy? · Tienes coche. → ¿<span class=\"vp-verb\">Tienes</span> coche? · Hablo inglés. → <span class=\"vp-prep\">No</span> <span class=\"vp-verb\">hablo</span> inglés.",
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "Spanish has no word like <em>do</em> or <em>does</em>. A statement becomes a question with your voice: <em>Vives aquí. → ¿Vives aquí?</em>",
        "tag": "No extra word"
      },
      {
        "html": "A named person can come before or after the verb: <em>¿Ana trabaja hoy?</em> or <em>¿Trabaja Ana hoy?</em> Both are correct.",
        "tag": "Word order"
      },
      {
        "html": "Written Spanish opens every question with <strong>¿</strong> and closes it with <strong>?</strong>: <em>¿Tienes tiempo?</em> The same goes for <strong>¡…!</strong>: <em>¡Hola!</em>",
        "tag": "¿ and ¡"
      },
      {
        "html": "Put <strong>no</strong> right before the verb: <em>No trabajo los lunes. Mi hijo no come carne.</em> Not after it: <em>Trabajo no.</em>",
        "tag": "no + verb"
      },
      {
        "html": "A short answer often needs two <em>no</em>: <em>¿Tienes hijos? – <strong>No, no</strong> tengo.</em> The first answers the question, and the second makes the verb negative. Also: <em>Sí, tengo dos.</em>",
        "tag": "Short answers"
      },
      {
        "html": "Add <strong>¿verdad?</strong> or <strong>¿no?</strong> to check something: <em>Vives aquí, ¿verdad?</em> <em>Es médica, ¿no?</em>",
        "tag": "¿verdad?"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>Vives aquí?</em> without the opening mark → ✓ <em>¿Vives aquí?</em> ✗ <em>Hablo no inglés</em> → ✓ <em>No hablo inglés</em>. ✗ <em>si</em> for “yes” → ✓ <em>sí</em> (<em>si</em> means “if”). With question words: <a href=\"/wh-questions\">Question words</a>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
      "tables": [
        {
          "caption": "Statement, question, negative",
          "head": ["Statement", "Question", "Negative"],
          "rows": [
            ["Vives aquí.", "¿Vives aquí?", "No vives aquí."],
            ["Tiene coche.", "¿Tiene coche?", "No tiene coche."],
            ["Son de Perú.", "¿Son de Perú?", "No son de Perú."],
            ["Hay leche.", "¿Hay leche?", "No hay leche."]
          ]
        },
        {
          "caption": "Short answers",
          "head": ["Question", "Yes", "No"],
          "rows": [
            ["¿Hablas español?", "Sí, hablo español.", "No, no hablo español."],
            ["¿Tienes hijos?", "Sí, tengo dos.", "No, no tengo."],
            ["¿Eres de aquí?", "Sí, soy de aquí.", "No, no soy de aquí."]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "boxes": [
        {
          "badge": "Careful: sí and si",
          "variant": "dat",
          "items": [
            "sí with an accent = yes.",
            "si without an accent = if."
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  },
